                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [S_1,S_2]
              is the set of action
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphisms"} homomorphisms
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intertwiners"} intertwiners
          %p
            Hence the inclusion of invariants into the conjugation action gives the inclusion of the external
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom+set"} hom set
            of the category of
            = succeed "-action" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mi Act
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi ρ
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi ρ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi ρ
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi ρ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  G Act(\rho_1,\rho_2)\hookrightarrow [\rho_1,\rho_2]
                  \\,.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Regarding the conjugation action as the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
              of actions immediately gives the generalization of this concept to more general kinds of actions, notably to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-actions"} infinity-actions
              in general
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-toposes"} (infinity,1)-toposes
              %em
                %a{:href => "infinity-action#CartesianClosedMonoidalStructure"} infinity-action – Conjugation action
              for more on this.
